THE EIGHTH JUDICIAL CIRCUIT OF FLORIDA 
ADMINISTRATIVE ORDER NO. 1.30 
 
ATTORNEY APPEARANCE AND WITHDRAWAL REQUIREMENTS FOR ALL CASES 
 
In order to provide for the fair, orderly, and efficient administration of justice in the 
Eighth Judicial Circuit and to ensure compliance with the Florida Rules of General Practice and 
Judicial Administration for those appearing before the court; and  
WHEREAS, Florida Rule of General Practice and Judicial Administration 2.505(e) states 
that an attorney may only appear in a judicial proceeding in one of three ways: (1) by filing 
and serving the first pleading or paper on behalf of a party in a proceeding; (2) by substitution 
of counsel, requiring written consent of the client, filed with the court, and a court order 
permitting substitution; or (3) by filing with the court and serving upon all parties a written 
notice of appearance for a previously pro se party, or as co-counsel for a party currently 
represented by counsel; 
WHEREAS, Florida Rule of Civil Procedure 1.041 provides that an attorney may file a 
limited notice of appearance limiting the attorney’s appearance to particular proceedings or 
specified matter; and 
WHEREAS, to terminate the limited appearance, a termination of limited appearance 
must be filed in accordance with Florida Rule of General Practice and Judicial Administration 
2.505; and 
WHEREAS, Florida Family Law Rule 12.040, though not applicable to civil cases, 
requires inclusion of the name, address, and telephone number of the person(s) represented 
by the withdrawing attorney, along with any designated e-mail address(es) for service, and 
Florida Family Law Rule of Procedure Form 12.900(d) provides a sample form for such notice, 
which serves as an acceptable format for use in civil cases (attached hereto as Appendix A); 
WHEREAS, Florida Rule of General Practice and Judicial Administration 2.505(f)(1)  
provides for the termination of appearance of an attorney by written order of the court after 

